---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="IB Physics Data Booklet Summary | Free Constants & Formulas"
  description="Complete IB Physics data booklet summary with all constants and formulas. Free download for IB Physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>IB Physics<br><span>Data Booklet Summary</span></h1>
    <p>All constants and formulas from the IB Physics data booklet. Quick reference for exams.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Physical Constants</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Fundamental Constants</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Constant</th><th>Value</th><th>Unit</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Speed of light (c)</td><td>3.00 × 10⁸</td><td>m s⁻¹</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Planck's constant (h)</td><td>6.63 × 10⁻³⁴</td><td>J s</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Elementary charge (e)</td><td>1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹</td><td>C</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Electron mass (mₑ)</td><td>9.11 × 10⁻³¹</td><td>kg</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Proton mass (mₚ)</td><td>1.67 × 10⁻²⁷</td><td>kg</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mechanics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Kinematics</h3>
        <pre><code>v = u + at
s = ut + ½at²
v² = u² + 2as
s = ½(u + v)t</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Forces</h3>
        <pre><code>F = ma
W = mg
F = kx (Hooke's law)
p = mv (momentum)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Energy</h3>
        <pre><code>KE = ½mv²
PE = mgh
Work = Fd cos θ
Power = W/t = Fv</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Waves</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Wave Equations</h3>
        <pre><code>v = fλ
T = 1/f
v = √(T/μ) (string)
v = √(B/ρ) (fluid)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Optics</h3>
        <pre><code>n₁ sin θ₁ = n₂ sin θ₂
1/f = 1/v + 1/u
M = -v/u (magnification)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Electricity</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Circuits</h3>
        <pre><code>V = IR (Ohm's law)
P = IV = I²R = V²/R
Rₛ = R₁ + R₂ + ... (series)
1/Rₚ = 1/R₁ + 1/R₂ + ... (parallel)</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Fields</h3>
        <pre><code>F = kQq/r² (Coulomb)
E = F/q = kQ/r²
V = Ed (uniform field)
C = Q/V = ε₀A/d</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
